The attached image is an immunoblot (Fig. 7D from the PDF) illustrating the processing and secretion of IL-1β by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). In the cell lysate, LPS and combined LPS + Nano-11 treatments show a strong band at approximately 30kD, corresponding to inactive pro-IL-1β. In the supernatant, Nano-11 alone, and more prominently Nano-11 combined with LPS priming, induce a distinct band at around 15-17kD. This confirms that Nano-11 promotes the cleavage of pro-IL-1β into its active, secreted 17kD form, particularly when BMDCs are primed with LPS, supporting its role as an immunostimulatory adjuvant.